    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d662">

                <pb facs="1134" n="1120" xml:id="pg1120"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/8–1244: Circular telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Australia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)<anchor n="52"
                        xml:id="d662-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-08-12T20:00:00-04:00">August 12, 1944—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Reference previous communications regarding refugee children. In view of the
                    situation in Hungary and the recent statement by Admiral Horthy that his
                    Government would grant exit permits to, and suspend deportations of, all Jewish
                    children for whom havens may be provided outside Hungary, would you request the
                    government to which you are accredited to extend its acceptance in principle to
                    children from Hungary as well as from France.</p>
                <p>You may assure appropriate officials of that government that no detailed plans
                    have as yet been developed for the actual immigration of refugee children into
                    its country. Should such plans become necessary at a later date, they will not
                    be developed without previous consultation with the government to which you are
                        accredited.<anchor n="53" xml:id="d662-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d662-f1" n="52" type="source" xml:id="d662-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated on the same date to Canada, the Dominican Republic, El Salvador,
                    Guatemala, Honduras, Ireland, Nicaragua, Paraguay, and Peru.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d662-f2" n="53" xml:id="d662-f2-content">
                <p>Governments accepting extension of this principle included Ireland, the Dominican
                    Republic, Honduras, Nicaragua, and Paraguay. Ecuador agreed to accept 300
                    European children and Brazil to receive 500 Jewish refugee children from
                    Hungary. Offers of asylum for Jewish children from Hungary were made also by
                    Sweden and Switzerland.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
